            <ArticleTitle>Acquisition of lytic spondylolisthesis in the adult.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>486-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Two adult patients are described with documented progression from a normally aligned spine to a lytic spondylolisthesis. In neither patient was the time of the pars fracture determined. Both patients complain of back pain with mild radicular symptoms.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
